# CDI — per-host configuration.
#
# FILL IN the values marked TODO by running the discovery commands in
# cluster/README.md on the machine. Everything here is host-specific; nothing
# below is guessed from a working CDI session.

CLUSTER_NAME="cdi"

# Modules to load, in order. Run `module avail` to see what exists.
# Leave the array empty if the host has no module system.
MODULES=(
  # TODO e.g. "python/3.11" "cuda/12.1"
)

# Where the virtualenv, caches, logs and the shared job queue live.
#
# This MUST be on the filesystem that every GPU machine sees, and it must be
# the same path on all of them. The default is a sibling of the repository,
# which is shared by construction - all the machines already read the code
# from there. $HOME is a bad default and was the old one: if home is local to
# each machine, every worker gets its own empty queue, every worker asks for
# a fresh `queue.sh init`, and the whole matrix runs again on each host.
#
# Point it somewhere else only if you have a scratch area that is also shared
# and has more room; the caches and checkpoints run to tens of gigabytes.
WORKDIR="${WORKDIR:-$(dirname "$REPO_DIR")/crusts-work}"

# Python to build the venv from, after the modules are loaded.
PYTHON_BIN="${PYTHON_BIN:-python3}"

# CUDA wheel index for torch. Check the node with nvidia-smi and read the
# "CUDA Version" in the header.
#
# torch>=2.6 is REQUIRED - transformers refuses to load unixcoder-base, which
# has no safetensors, on anything older (CVE-2025-32434). Not every index
# carries a new enough build:
#
#   cu118  up to 2.7.1    ok, for pre-Pascal devices
#   cu121  up to 2.5.1    TOO OLD - never use this one
#   cu124  up to 2.6.0    ok, only just
#   cu126  up to 2.14.0   default; kernels for sm_50..sm_90 only
#   cu128  up to 2.11.0   older torch, avoid unless a device needs it
#   cu130  up to 2.14.0   CUDA 13; needed for Blackwell sm_120
#   cu132  up to 2.14.0   CUDA 13.2
#
# The index caps BOTH the torch version and the GPU architectures. cu126 is
# the default because it carries the newest torch, but it has no Blackwell
# kernels - see cluster/config/pitu.env.
#
# CUDA 12.x drivers are minor-version compatible, so a 12.x driver generally
# runs any cu12x build - cu126 is the safe default on any CUDA 12 node.
# Set to "cpu" to force a CPU-only build.
TORCH_CUDA="${TORCH_CUDA:-cu126}"     # TODO confirm against nvidia-smi

# Batch size and epochs are NOT set here. They are experiment-wide and live in
# cluster/common.sh: the InfoNCE loss uses in-batch negatives, so a host that
# raised the batch to fill a bigger GPU would produce results incomparable
# with every other host. Only hardware settings belong in this file.

# Pin to specific GPUs if the host is shared. Empty means "use what torch sees".
# export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0
